FriendFlix media server image (trial)
=====================================

This image is the Ferrofin server image

  ghcr.io/mangoleaf/ferrofin:v1.5.2
  sha256:c00fe34634d7f886888c027cd0552d990a4c9cd918b45c2fce96d5963aca26d5

with the numbered changes listed in mediaserver/README.md of https://github.com/LetsManu/friendflix
(built from mediaserver/Dockerfile there). Each change is also offered to the Ferrofin project.

Ferrofin
  A Rust re-implementation of the Jellyfin server API. Copyright its authors.
  Licence: GNU General Public License v3.0 only (GPL-3.0-only).
  Source: https://github.com/mangoleaf/ferrofin, tag v1.5.2. This image does not change Ferrofin's source code: the
  ferrofin-server binary is the one in the image above, built by the Ferrofin project from that tag.

Also in the base image (unchanged, licences as shipped by their projects)
  jellyfin-ffmpeg8 (GPL-3.0, /usr/lib/jellyfin-ffmpeg), 7zip (LGPL-2.1+ with the unRAR restriction) and Debian's non-free
  7zip-rar (its RAR decoder, unRAR licence; Ferrofin runs 7z as a separate program for RAR comic covers), Debian trixie
  packages (each under /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright), and jellyfin-web (GPL-2.0): change 0004 removes it from the image's file system
  (/usr/share/ferrofin/web), but its files are still in the base image's layer.

Added by FriendFlix, change 0001 (Intel OpenCL runtime, amd64 only)
  Intel compute-runtime (NEO) 26.35.39758.10 and 24.35.30872.36 (legacy) - MIT, https://github.com/intel/compute-runtime
  Intel Graphics Compiler 2.41.5 and 1.0.17537.24 (legacy) - MIT, https://github.com/intel/intel-graphics-compiler
  Intel Graphics Memory Management Library (gmmlib) 22.10.0 - MIT, https://github.com/intel/gmmlib
  Unchanged release packages from those projects; their bundled third-party parts keep their own licences (see
  /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright where the package ships one, and the projects' LICENSE files).

FriendFlix's own build files (mediaserver/Dockerfile, try.sh, probe.sh) are AGPL-3.0-or-later; they are not part of this
image. Corresponding source for the GPL parts: the URLs and tags above.
